// Sync service location.
//
// These two values are not secrets. The anon key is a public client identifier;
// every row it can reach is gated by row level security, and the payloads behind
// that gate are encrypted with a per-circle key this project never holds.
//
// The host is stored without its scheme on purpose: xcconfig treats "//" as the
// start of a comment, so "https://example.com" would be truncated. Info.plist
// rebuilds the URL as https://$(SUPABASE_HOST).
//
// Leave the placeholders in place to build a device-only app with syncing off.
// To point a build at a real project, either edit Supabase.local.xcconfig
// (untracked) or override SUPABASE_HOST and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in CI.

SUPABASE_HOST = YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = YOUR_ANON_KEY

#include? "Supabase.local.xcconfig"
